 ## Overview
-Final Composition is a volume rendering technique that integrates voxel data into a 2D image by defining organs via intensity ranges and applying lighting to depict surfaces [S1, unofficial]. It distinguishes itself from pure segmentation methods by incorporating the entire volume's information while avoiding exact boundary determination, and from pure projection methods by using illumination to enhance surface perception [S1, unofficial]. It is primarily chosen when organ surface visualization is required without arbitrary thresholding [S1, unofficial].
